egl/gbm: a window surface of the config's channel sizes, as the TV's Mali.

LG's Qt EGLFS Starfish plugin of the ponytail releases takes the first config eglChooseConfig gives
for its alpha-8 surface format and creates the gbm_surface in the output's configured format,
abgr8888. W23A ponytail's Mali driver (33.31.66, bsppart libmali.so.0.1) lists its GBM window
configs XR24, AR24, RG16, ... (gbm_get_configs), so the plugin gets the ARGB8888 config for an
ABGR8888 surface; the driver's config_compatible_with_format compares the config's red, green,
blue and alpha sizes with the format's (as r46p0's and r51's do), and the set draws. Mesa requires
compatible formats, refuses the pair with EGL_BAD_MATCH, and the compositor aborts in a loop.

Where the gl layer names the TV driver's GBM window formats (/usr/share/beanjar/gbm-window-formats,
a Mali GBM winsys), an RGB surface format whose channel sizes are the config's is compatible too.
The surface's buffers keep its own format, which the renderer draws into. Without the file nothing
changes.
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
@@ -129,6 +129,23 @@
        util_is_format_compatible(fmt_s, fmt_c))
       return true;
 
+   /* The emulated TV's Mali driver (Beanjar's gl layer names its GBM window
+    * formats) accepts a window surface whose format has the config's channel
+    * sizes, whatever their order (libmali config_compatible_with_format), so
+    * a client may render with an ARGB8888 config to an ABGR8888 surface. */
+   if (access("/usr/share/beanjar/gbm-window-formats", R_OK) == 0 &&
+       fmt_c->colorspace == UTIL_FORMAT_COLORSPACE_RGB &&
+       fmt_s->colorspace == UTIL_FORMAT_COLORSPACE_RGB) {
+      for (unsigned c = 0; c < 4; c++) {
+         if (util_format_get_component_bits(gl_config->color_format,
+                                            UTIL_FORMAT_COLORSPACE_RGB, c) !=
+             util_format_get_component_bits(visual->pipe_format,
+                                            UTIL_FORMAT_COLORSPACE_RGB, c))
+            return false;
+      }
+      return true;
+   }
+
    return false;
 }
 
